nvgpu: build for Linux 7.x

Kernel API changes between v6.18 and v7.3. Each change is gated on the
kernel version, so older kernels build the same code as before.

- v7.2 removed strncpy(). nvgpu relies on its exact semantics (bounded
  copy, zero padding, no forced terminator) in a dozen places, so a
  force-included header provides it.
- v7.1 renamed zap_vma_ptes() to zap_special_vma_range().
- v7.1 removed <linux/of_gpio.h> and of_get_named_gpio(); look the GPIO
  up through fwnode_gpiod_get_index() and keep using its number.
- v7.1 removed clk_ops.round_rate; use determine_rate.

